WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:18.384
One morning after breakfast, a young man came into the stable with Farmer Grey.

2
00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:24.546
"Here he is," my master said, stopping in front of my stall.

3
00:00:25.266 --> 00:00:26.547
The stranger peered in at me.

4
00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.907
"What a handsome horse.

5
00:00:29.287 --> 00:00:31.388
I'm not surprised the squire chose him."

6
00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:36.030
"Yes, I'm sure he'll enjoy this horse," Farmer Grey said.

7
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.431
"I will certainly miss him when he goes."

8
00:00:41.673 --> 00:00:43.814
The farmer led me out and gave me a pat.

9
00:00:45.135 --> 00:00:48.437
I didn't understand what was going on, or why his eyes looked sad.

10
00:00:49.478 --> 00:00:52.239
But I put my nose into his hand to try to make him feel better.

11
00:00:52.259 --> 00:00:56.562
"Good-bye, boy," my master said.

12
00:00:56.582 --> 00:00:59.103
"Be a good horse, and always do your best."

13
00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:03.525
Then he handed my lead rope to the other man.

14
00:01:04.546 --> 00:01:06.887
The stranger and I walked out through the farm gates.

15
00:01:08.027 --> 00:01:11.289
My mother and some of the other horses neighed to me from the pasture.

16
00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:19.713
Soon we turned in through another gate, and I saw a fine estate.

17
00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:22.754
This was my new home, Birtwick Park.

18
00:01:23.715 --> 00:01:28.504
The man leading me was James, the head groom.

19
00:01:28.524 --> 00:01:31.687
He put me into a large, airy stall and gave me a handful of grain.

20
00:01:31.707 --> 00:01:35.430
"There you go," he said kindly.

21
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.032
"I'd better go tell the squire you're here."

22
00:01:40.995 --> 00:01:44.618
There were four stalls in this part of the stable, and mine was the largest.

23
00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:48.661
In a smaller stall stood a fat, gray pony.

24
00:01:50.223 --> 00:01:52.725
He had a thick mane and tail, and a pretty head.

25
00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.187
"Hello," I said.

26
00:01:55.207 --> 00:01:56.388
"What's your name?"

27
00:01:57.756 --> 00:01:59.758
"I'm Merrylegs," the pony said.

28
00:01:59.778 --> 00:02:05.481
"I am very handsome so the young ladies love to ride me or drive me in a cart.

29
00:02:06.722 --> 00:02:08.644
Are you going to live next door to me now?"

30
00:02:08.664 --> 00:02:11.706
"I think so," I answered.

31
00:02:11.726 --> 00:02:15.749
"I hope you're a nice horse," Merrylegs said.

32
00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:19.191
"I don't like living next door to anyone who bites."

33
00:02:20.772 --> 00:02:22.673
He looked over at the stall on his other side.

34
00:02:23.474 --> 00:02:26.236
A chestnut mare with a long, graceful neck stood there.

35
00:02:28.728 --> 00:02:31.571
"So you're the one who took my stall," she snapped.

36
00:02:31.591 --> 00:02:34.553
"How dare you put a lady out of her home!"

37
00:02:36.054 --> 00:02:39.377
"Excuse me, but I did no such thing," I said politely.

38
00:02:39.397 --> 00:02:42.820
"The man who brought me here put me in this stall.

39
00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.782
I truly had no choice in the matter."

40
00:02:46.904 --> 00:02:51.027
"Don't worry about her," Merrylegs said quietly as the mare turned away.

41
00:02:51.047 --> 00:02:56.652
"Ginger knows it's her own fault she was moved out of that stall.

42
00:02:57.852 --> 00:03:02.835
She has a bad habit of biting, and the young ladies were becoming afraid to visit me."

43
00:03:02.855 --> 00:03:07.038
"They won't have to worry about me," I said.

44
00:03:07.058 --> 00:03:10.840
"The only things I bite are grass, hay, and grain.

45
00:03:11.781 --> 00:03:12.882
Why does Ginger bite?"

46
00:03:13.942 --> 00:03:17.685
"She says no one was ever nice to her before," Merrylegs said.

47
00:03:17.705 --> 00:03:22.708
"John and James hope she'll be better tempered now that she's here."

48
00:03:26.656 --> 00:03:29.317
The next day John Manly led me out of my stall.

49
00:03:30.178 --> 00:03:31.378
John was the head coachman.

50
00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:34.860
James and the other stable hands worked for him.

51
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.441
John had kind eyes and a calm manner.

52
00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:42.903
He groomed me from head to hoof, making my dark coat gleam.

53
00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:46.084
He was almost finished when the squire arrived.

54
00:03:46.104 --> 00:03:49.726
"Hello, John," the squire said.

55
00:03:49.746 --> 00:03:54.748
"I wanted to try out my new horse this morning, but I'm too busy.

56
00:03:55.532 --> 00:03:58.274
Would you ride him for me and let me know how he goes?"

57
00:03:58.294 --> 00:04:01.096
"Of course, sir," John said.

58
00:04:02.477 --> 00:04:04.438
He brought out a saddle along with a bridle.

59
00:04:05.719 --> 00:04:08.481
When he set the saddle on my back, it pinched my shoulders.

60
00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.843
Luckily John immediately saw that it didn't fit.

61
00:04:12.904 --> 00:04:14.625
He took it away and brought out a different one.

62
00:04:17.647 --> 00:04:21.490
John was a very good rider, and I was happy to do exactly what he asked.

63
00:04:23.031 --> 00:04:25.392
We walked for a while, and then we trotted.

64
00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.594
Finally he urged me into a fast gallop.

65
00:04:30.615 --> 00:04:34.656
We were riding back toward the stable when we passed the squire walking with his wife.

66
00:04:34.676 --> 00:04:36.837
"How was your ride, John?"

67
00:04:37.217 --> 00:04:38.057
the squire asked.

68
00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:41.759
"Very good, sir," John answered, sounding pleased.

69
00:04:41.779 --> 00:04:45.861
"It's obvious the horse has been well-treated and well-trained."

70
00:04:46.981 --> 00:04:48.682
"Excellent," the squire said.

71
00:04:48.702 --> 00:04:50.602
"I'll try him myself tomorrow."

72
00:04:52.103 --> 00:04:54.164
The next day the squire took his turn on me.

73
00:04:54.624 --> 00:04:57.366
He was a good rider too, and we had a pleasant ride.

74
00:04:59.988 --> 00:05:02.149
When we passed the house, his wife came out.

75
00:05:04.471 --> 00:05:05.411
"How do you like him?"

76
00:05:05.852 --> 00:05:06.372
she asked.

77
00:05:06.392 --> 00:05:10.375
"I've never ridden a finer horse," the squire replied.

78
00:05:10.395 --> 00:05:13.017
"Now all this fellow needs is a name."

79
00:05:14.378 --> 00:05:17.139
"Should we call him Blackbird, like your uncle's old horse?"

80
00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.380
his wife asked.

81
00:05:19.741 --> 00:05:20.842
The squire shook his head.

82
00:05:20.862 --> 00:05:23.224
"He is handsomer than Blackbird ever was."

83
00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.666
"He really is a beauty," his wife agreed.

84
00:05:27.686 --> 00:05:30.687
"We could call him Black Beauty."

85
00:05:30.707 --> 00:05:34.429
"Black Beauty," the squire said thoughtfully.

86
00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:35.790
"I like it."

87
00:05:37.191 --> 00:05:39.652
And so I had a new home and a new name.
